{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_420132660", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Sam Panopoulos, an 81-year-old Greek-Canadian, claimed to have invented the Hawaiian pizza in 1962.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_565495028#0_805615245"]}, {"text": "The invention occurred in Chatham, Ontario, where pizza was not widely known at that time.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_565495028#0_805615245"]}, {"text": "Panopoulos used canned pineapple, a common household item in Ontario due to Tiki culture and advertising by grocery stores.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_565495028#0_805615245"]}, {"text": "The Hawaiian pizza quickly gained popularity, becoming one of the most controversial entries in the pizza lexicon.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_565495028#0_805615245"]}, {"text": "The combination of ham and pineapple was an accident, resulting from limited toppings available at the time.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_565495028#0_805615245"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1440134319", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Instant noodles are high in fat, salt, and calories, which can contribute to weight gain and other health issues.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_228347930#2_517499860"]}, {"text": "TBHQ is a chemical preservative used in instant noodles that can be toxic in large doses.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1274150155#3_2795426812", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1515391350#1_3157248657"]}, {"text": "Studies have shown that prolonged exposure to high doses of TBHQ may be carcinogenic, though some studies suggest it could prevent cancer.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1274150155#3_2795426812"]}, {"text": "A study found that women who ate more than two portions of instant noodles per week had a higher chance of developing metabolic syndrome, linked to heart conditions and diabetes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_622734099#6_1088070513"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_300872161", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article mentions that CIA officers Mark McFarlin and another unnamed officer resigned or faced disciplinary action following an incident where a ton of cocaine was accidentally shipped to the U.S. from Venezuela in 1986.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2640991387#2_2923193035"]}, {"text": "The alleged CIA involvement in Contra cocaine trafficking took place during the 1980s Nicaraguan civil war, as stated in the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2640991387#2_2923193035"]}, {"text": "According to the article, DEA field agent Hector Berrellez claimed that CIA contract workers brought drugs into the U.S. and landed them at government air bases.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2640991387#2_2923193035"]}, {"text": "The 2006 document 'Undercover Armies: CIA and Surrogate Warfare in Laos' was released following a FOIA request, as mentioned in the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1279654714#3_2091505668"]}, {"text": "Gary Webb's 1996 series claimed that CIA involvement played a role in creating the crack cocaine problem in the U.S., as stated in the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2640991387#2_2923193035"]}, {"text": "The Kerry Committee found that Contra drug links included payments to drug traffickers using funds authorized for humanitarian assistance to the Contras, as mentioned in the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2640991387#2_2923193035"]}, {"text": "The article states that multiple government bodies, including the House of Representatives, Senate, Department of Justice, and the CIA's Office of the Inspector General, investigated the alleged CIA involvement in Contra cocaine trafficking.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2640991387#2_2923193035"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_116067546", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Quantum computers could crack Bitcoin by 2022, according to some experts.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_820742678#1_1612701707"]}, {"text": "A 4,000 qubit quantum computer could theoretically crack Bitcoin's encryption in a matter of seconds.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_820742678#1_1612701707"]}, {"text": "Google announced a quantum computer with 54 qubits in October 2019, which is currently the most powerful publicly known quantum computer.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_820742678#1_1612701707"]}, {"text": "Andersen Cheng predicts that a quantum computer could be used to crack Bitcoin's code within two years, based on intelligence world evidence.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_820742678#1_1612701707"]}, {"text": "Microsoft has contributed to both software and hardware aspects of quantum computing through various initiatives.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1398779806#5_1575306476"]}, {"text": "Andersen Cheng dismisses concerns that a quantum computer would need to be purpose-built for cracking Bitcoin's code, stating people know exactly what to do but lack the power to execute it.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_820742678#1_1612701707"]}, {"text": "The National Institute for Standards and Technology (NIST) is running a competition to create post-quantum cryptographic algorithms, which could determine the future of blockchain security against quantum computers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_820742678#1_1612701707"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_861891150", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article mentions that MSCHF, the company behind the Satan Shoes, sold Jesus-themed shoes in 2019.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181289058#2_375784928"]}, {"text": "According to the article, Lil Nas X has tweeted responses to posts about the Satan Shoes, defending them as part of his recent music video theme.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181289058#1_375783647"]}, {"text": "The article states that MSCHF is partnering with Lil Nas X to offer 666 pairs of Satan Shoes for one day only, which were announced as going on sale on March 29.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_894616096#0_1783952733"]}, {"text": "Nike has filed a lawsuit against MSCHF over trademark infringement related to the Satan Shoes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_202036904#4_426809461"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1648697797", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The methodology lacks clear strategies to ensure reliability in studies about celebrity cannibalistic fantasies from unverified social media.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249144097#5_450782082"]}, {"text": "Steps include verifying claims through cross-referencing and fact-checking.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_30_1915228227#3_3973679616"]}, {"text": "Historians should evaluate social media posts using source criticism principles.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1192013567#1_2436953508"]}, {"text": "Key research elements involve robust data collection, analysis, and verification.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_182657652#10_407154003"]}, {"text": "Accuracy can be ensured by employing rigorous data quality management techniques.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_127339060#1_301036651"]}, {"text": "Using only social media risks misinformation; integrating multiple sources mitigates this.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_182657652#3_407135084"]}, {"text": "Effective integration of evidence from various sources enhances understanding.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_182657652#12_407159933"]}, {"text": "Ethical considerations include privacy, harm avoidance, and transparency in research.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1211280373#5_2411383964"]}, {"text": "Clear, transparent communication is crucial for public engagement.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_182657652#11_407156954"]}, {"text": "Suitable analysis methods include qualitative content and thematic analysis.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249169957#6_450850586"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_481628070", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The Supreme Court case could present a direct challenge to Roe v. Wade, the 1973 landmark Supreme Court decision legalizing abortion nationwide prior to viability.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_735489699#6_936631848"]}, {"text": "The ruling potentially coming in the middle of the 2022 midterm elections could have significant political implications.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_735489699#6_936631848"]}, {"text": "The case will be a blockbuster one, with the justices revisiting an issue that still deeply divides the country some fifty years after the landmark opinion.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_735489699#6_936631848"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_501708725", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article discusses a controversy where Gen Z attempts to cancel Eminem, but millennials defend him.", "citations": []}, {"text": "Millennials argue that they grew up with Eminem's music and find his lyrics not as offensive as some Gen Z members claim.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_603633527#7_1145159414"]}, {"text": "Eminem's 2010 hit 'Love the Way You Lie' features a verse that some Gen Z members argue glorifies violence against women.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_142902213#1_142277555"]}, {"text": "The article mentions that Rihanna has stated the verse was actually a condemnation of domestic abuse rather than a celebration.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_142902213#1_142277555"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_502424913", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The US government is reportedly gearing up to share information about the 'reality' of UFOs with the public, according to a whistleblower.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1301089740#11_1985347298"]}, {"text": "The upcoming report touches down on unexplainable details such as tic-tac-shaped objects, cubes within spheres, and mysterious black triangles.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1301089740#11_1985347298"]}, {"text": "The existence of the AATIP wasn't revealed until 2017, along with a 'chill of a video' montage captured by the Navy featuring a dark circular object flying in front of a military jet.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1301089740#11_1985347298"]}, {"text": "The Pentagon officially released three videos taken by US Navy pilots showing mid-air encounters with what appear to be UFOs, indicating the nature of the reported phenomena.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1301089740#11_1985347298"]}, {"text": "The report is scheduled for release but no specific date or committee has been mentioned in the provided information.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1301089740#11_1985347298"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_2529216", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The original Novaya Gazeta report on the Blue Whale Challenge was criticized for lacking credible data and balance.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248491773#7_563385793", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_4199697#1_9231914"]}, {"text": "There were no direct evidence found linking over 100 teen suicides to the Blue Whale Challenge game.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_4199697#10_9245328", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_793744896#0_1357166275"]}, {"text": "Investigative journalist Evgeny Berg discovered that many of the 'curators' in the online groups were children aged 12 to 14 who were copying parts of a reported game rather than creating it.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2413955574#4_2670753539", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_180864473#1_374771687"]}, {"text": "The individual arrested in connection with the Blue Whale Challenge confessed to creating the game but later charges were dropped except for one.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2413955574#0_2670745617", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_846026353#15_1813980893"]}, {"text": "People's dependence on smartphones and modern technology could bring about the coming of the Antichrist according to the leader of the Russian Orthodox Church.", "citations": []}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_7751734", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Carlos Ghosn, the former boss of Nissan, managed to leave Japan where he was awaiting trial.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1276206716#0_2733570273"]}, {"text": "He posted 1bn yen (\u00a36.8m; $8.9m) in bail in April, was monitored by a 24-hour camera outside his house, and had his use of technology heavily restricted.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1276206716#0_2733570273"]}, {"text": "On 8 January, in his first public comments since fleeing, Mr Ghosn refused to say how he managed to leave Japan, joking that it was a 'mission impossible'.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1276206716#0_2733570273"]}, {"text": "Reports suggest that Mr Ghosn left his house and walked about 800m to a nearby hotel in the middle of the afternoon on 29 December, where he joined two men thought to be Americans.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1276206716#0_2733570273"]}, {"text": "The Wall Street Journal reported that a team was carefully assembled to carry out the plot, including accomplices in Japan who transported Mr Ghosn onto a private jet bound for Istanbul.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1276206716#0_2733570273"]}, {"text": "Questions remain about the documents Mr Ghosn used to enter Lebanon, as he holds three passports - Brazilian, French and Lebanese.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1276206716#0_2733570273"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_441326441", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Scientists are criticizing a report suggesting microwave attacks could have caused \u201cHavana Syndrome\u201d in US diplomats, stating it does not make a coherent argument for microwaves being involved.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_358186207#2_621417445"]}, {"text": "The National Academies of Sciences report commissioned by the US State Department found that while a microwave attack is the \u201cmost plausible\u201d explanation, it remains far from conclusive.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_358186207#2_621417445"]}, {"text": "Experts in microwaves and group psychology dismissed the microwave theory as implausible or even \u201cscience fiction,\u201d highlighting concerns about the scientific basis of the findings.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_358186207#2_621417445", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_3782292837#0_3889522283"]}, {"text": "The Cuban Neuroscience Center also criticized the report's conclusions on microwaves, suggesting that early injuries likely spread through mass psychology rather than a targeted attack.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_358186207#2_621417445"]}, {"text": "Old Dominion University bioengineer Andrei Pakhomov, a Russian emigre, expressed skepticism about the microwave theory based on his four decades of research in the area.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_358186207#2_621417445"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1300032609", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "A conservatorship is legally defined as a court-appointed individual or organization to care for someone unable to manage their own affairs.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_924469944#12_1994682377"]}, {"text": "Jamie Spears was granted conservatorship in 2008 after Britney's mental health issues, making it permanent in 2009.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1570538012#14_2911995503"]}, {"text": "Britney's legal team seeks Jodi Montgomery and Bessemer Trust as her permanent conservators.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249135213#0_450752264"]}, {"text": "Jamie argues his conservatorship has benefited Britney\u2019s estate, valuing it over $60 million.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1570538012#14_2911995503"]}, {"text": "The #FreeBritney movement supports Britney\u2019s desire to leave the conservatorship, with fans protesting and using social media.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249135213#0_450752264"]}, {"text": "Bessemer Trust was appointed co-conservator but details of their management are not provided.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1292466165#1_2369928850"]}, {"text": "Britney's legal team has expanded, though specifics about new attorneys' experience are not detailed.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249135213#0_450752264"]}, {"text": "#FreeBritney highlights Britney's case, affecting her daily life and career without clear impact explanation.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249135213#0_450752264"]}, {"text": "Stakeholders include Bessemer Trust, Jodi Montgomery, and Jamie Spears, but their roles are not fully explained.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249135213#0_450752264"]}, {"text": "Britney\u2019s conservatorship affects her personal and professional life, with ongoing legal battles.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249135213#0_450752264"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_227081897", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article discusses the Blackout Challenge on TikTok, which has led to at least one child's death and another fighting for their life.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_557526820#4_1019685708"]}, {"text": "Experts warn that participating in such challenges can lead to severe consequences, including brain damage or death.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_500352179#0_984884991", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_500352179#1_984887400"]}, {"text": "The article suggests that TikTok's safety measures may not be sufficient to protect users from engaging in harmful challenges like the Blackout Challenge.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_557526820#4_1019685708", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_500352179#0_984884991"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1014551192", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The documentary focuses on Rick Singer, the mastermind behind the largest college admissions scandal in history.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_602165982#4_834615499"]}, {"text": "Singer's scheme involved facilitating cheating on ACT and SAT exams, as well as bribing college athletics directors with donations.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_602165982#4_834615499"]}, {"text": "While many of the parents and college employees indicted in the scandal have been charged and sentenced, Singer is yet to be sentenced.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_602165982#4_834615499"]}, {"text": "Singer collected $25 million from clients who paid to guarantee admission at elite colleges and universities through his Key Worldwide Foundation.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_602165982#4_834615499"]}, {"text": "The documentary highlights that Singer's cooperation with investigators led to a lesser sentence, but his sentencing date remains uncertain.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_602165982#4_834615499"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1165221603", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Oxygen bars and recreational oxygen inhalers promise to improve your well-being, but the health claims are questionable.", "citations": []}, {"text": "Healthy individuals do not need extra oxygen as humans have evolved to live in an atmosphere with 21 percent oxygen.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_303278851#1_614451522"]}, {"text": "Athletes might benefit from supplemental oxygen during intense exercise, but this is not applicable to the average individual.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_303278851#1_614451522"]}, {"text": "The cleanliness of equipment at oxygen bars is a concern as there is no standardization or oversight to ensure sterility.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_573008162#2_1116838137"]}, {"text": "Using scented oxygen in oxygen bars could pose a risk for people with asthma or other lung conditions due to potential allergic reactions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_969015618#7_1695639649"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1960853470", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Cancer researchers in Israel have found that cannabinoids can kill brain and breast cancer cells, but additional research is needed to fully understand their effectiveness.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_250609978#3_607980444"]}, {"text": "Doctors at the UCSF Osher Center for Integrative Medicine caution against assuming that cannabis is a cure, citing the lack of large-scale clinical trials to support this claim.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_1410960902#11_2373827672"]}, {"text": "While anecdotal accounts suggest that some patients have experienced complete recovery after using cannabis, doctors advise against relying solely on these stories for treatment decisions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_122645132#18_224182660"]}, {"text": "The National Academies of Sciences, Engineering and Medicine found insufficient evidence to recommend cannabis as a direct treatment for cancer without large-scale clinical trials.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_603374908#3_1083853233"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_654618974", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The Mandela Effect occurs when a large group of people believe an event occurred when it did not, as seen in examples like the Berenstein Bears vs. The Berenstain Bears and 'I am your father' from Star Wars.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_578980629#0_1133015537"]}, {"text": "Doctors believe the Mandela effect is a form of confabulation, where people create false memories without intending to lie or deceive others.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_481189496#0_959409935"]}, {"text": "False memories can be influenced by factors such as eyewitness testimony and digital alterations of images, logos, and sayings.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1210906276#2_2410419971"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_1430382251", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article suggests that future versions of BrainEx could complicate organ donation decisions by potentially expanding the donor pool, as revived cellular function might indicate a longer window for viability.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_272210287#1_510412181"]}, {"text": "Kevin Cmunt, CEO of Gift of Hope, one of the United States\u2019s largest organ donation networks, does not see BrainEx as a major disruption to current practices in organ donation.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_1413689018#3_2936541225"]}, {"text": "The article mentions that BrainEx could potentially improve organ donations by giving medical professionals an even greater imperative to maintain circulation, which could make organs more viable for donation than they would be otherwise.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_1413689018#3_2936541225"]}, {"text": "The article states that BrainEx could complicate organ donation decisions by blurring the lines of brain death, which could have significant ethical and philosophical implications for understanding consciousness.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_4067137#3_8895196"]}, {"text": "The article does not provide specific data or studies supporting the claim that BrainEx could significantly extend the viability of organs for transplantation, but it mentions that future versions might have such benefits.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_272210287#1_510412181"]}, {"text": "The article suggests that future versions of BrainEx could have significant long-term benefits for medical research and clinical applications, as it allows for the study of brain function after death in a way not previously possible.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_272210287#1_510412181"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_273997000", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Citibank wired $900 million in a 'clerical error', which has plunged the bank into legal battles with Revlon's lenders and investment funds.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_550772505#12_1305085701"]}, {"text": "Citibank has launched an internal investigation into the matter, but a spokeswoman declined to comment.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_900269694#5_1940850929"]}, {"text": "Several hedge funds are refusing to hand back the $900 million, citing a lawsuit against Revlon for defaulting on its loan.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_737837679#11_1576185857"]}, {"text": "The incident is one of the biggest screw-ups on Wall Street in ages and has set tongues wagging in financial markets.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1131253898#1_2392408248"]}, {"text": "Citibank's stock price may have been affected by the unauthorized transfer, though no specific impact was mentioned.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1209863788#10_2398932334"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_515083157", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "NASA scientists claim to have discovered evidence of a parallel universe where time moves backwards.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#8_1610055324"]}, {"text": "The ANITA experiment, using electronic antennas high above Antarctica, detected particles that may be moving backwards in time.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#8_1610055324"]}, {"text": "Peter Gorham, a physics professor at the University of Hawaii, suggested that signals came from upward-moving particles tunneling through the Earth before erupting from the ice.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#8_1610055324"]}, {"text": "However, not everyone is convinced by these results; Geraint Lewis, an astrophysicist at the University of Sydney, stated that alternative ideas are still on the table.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#8_1610055324"]}, {"text": "Pat Scott, an astroparticle phenomenologist at the University of Queensland, said that while the theory was 'plausible', there were myriad of other theories that could account for ANITA's detections.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#8_1610055324"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_515287844", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The fire at Notre-Dame Cathedral started around 6:50 PM local time on Monday night, or 2:50 AM AEST.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_211327330#11_518660289"]}, {"text": "French authorities initially suggested that the fire might be linked to ongoing renovations at the cathedral, but arson was ruled out by prosecutors.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_211327330#11_518660289", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1295344469#5_3015848824"]}, {"text": "The spire of Notre-Dame collapsed during the fire, causing significant damage to the iconic structure.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_211327330#11_518660289"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_730773621", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Belle Delphine's estimated net worth is around half a million dollars, according to Dreshare.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_1002310044#9_1980727883"]}, {"text": "Belle Delphine was born in South Africa and moved to the U.K. at age 9, where she discovered the internet.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_211921582#1_485621851"]}, {"text": "Belle Delphine was a 14-year-old dropout who started hustling at age 13, holding various odd jobs including being a waitress and working at a coffee shop.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_296934542#5_749515109"]}, {"text": "Belle Delphine launched her career on Instagram in 2018, initially posting vaguely NSFW content before gaining notoriety for a fake account on an adult video website.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_745485860#17_1410767596"]}, {"text": "Belle Delphine earned around $50,000 a year via her Patreon alone, with an average patron spending $12 per month.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_1002310044#9_1980727883"]}, {"text": "Belle Delphine angered the masses when she trolled her fans with a fake account on an adult video website, uploading 12 videos that were mostly PG content.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2250946488#12_2490792076"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1289995263", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Graham Ivan Clark, a 17-year-old from Florida, was arrested for the Twitter hack.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_308653026#0_707048499"]}, {"text": "The hack involved multiple individuals, including Graham Ivan Clark, Mason John Sheppard, and Nima Fazeli.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_308653026#0_707048499"]}, {"text": "The hackers broke into 130 Twitter accounts during the incident.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_308653026#0_707048499"]}, {"text": "Twitter stated that they were embarrassed by the hack, which called into question their security measures.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_308653026#0_707048499"]}, {"text": "Graham Ivan Clark was charged with 30 felony charges, including fraud, and faces legal action as an adult.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_308653026#0_707048499"]}, {"text": "Clark convinced a Twitter employee to provide him with credentials, allowing access to customer service portals.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_308653026#0_707048499"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_5-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1666095905", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The proposed European Super League would significantly impact the prospects for smaller clubs competing in international football competitions, as it could undermine the pyramid philosophy that exists in European soccer.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_643927135#0_1326928286"]}, {"text": "The European Super League's estimated annual value is $2 billion, per J.P. Morgan.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#8_656741989"]}, {"text": "According to FIFA, players from clubs involved in the proposed European Super League could face restrictions or bans from international competitions if it were established.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_83725357#0_161674380"]}, {"text": "Some of the main criticisms against the proposed European Super League include concerns over its impact on smaller clubs and grassroots football, as well as allegations of prioritizing financial gain over sporting merit.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1632305306#0_1835809112"]}, {"text": "The establishment of the proposed European Super League could affect the UEFA Champions League by potentially reducing its prestige and competitiveness due to the exclusion of top clubs from Europe's premier club competition.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#3_3112397911"]}, {"text": "The proposed ESL claims to offer significant economic benefits, including long-term commitment to uncapped solidarity payments that will grow in line with league revenues.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_47598423#1_104380199"]}, {"text": "The establishment of the proposed ESL could have significant long-term impacts on the overall structure and governance of international football, potentially leading to a fragmented and less unified global football landscape.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2325498762#3_2620311403"]}, {"text": "The official stance of the Premier League regarding the proposed ESL is negative, with UK Prime Minister Boris Johnson stating that they will look at everything possible to prevent it from happening.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2472183859#9_2735767163"]}, {"text": "The establishment of the proposed ESL could affect the global fan base and the overall popularity of football by potentially alienating fans who support traditional club structures and values.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2472183859#10_2735769188"]}]}
